Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: modload_load_given() loading the bytes it is given: it fetches a module of that name from bootstrap instead, as chora did before #964, and the module that runs is whatever the pool holds under the name and not what the HAL checked.  modload_test's [5] gives modload_a/only_a.so's bytes as modload_given/only_a.so, which bootstrap does not have, and gets nothing.
Run: --iommu intel --edu --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: modload_test: \[5\] modload_load_given\(\) of modload_a/only_a.so.s [0-9]+ bytes, as modload_given/only_a.so, gave nothing, where modload_a/only_a.so a was given -- WRONG
Note: a chora still drives its device here, its module's name being in the bundle's pool: the same bytes as those given, which is why only a pool bootstrap lacks can tell the two apart.

